NODE id=github.com/paxlabs-inc/layerx/internal/store.Store.EnsureTransferPartitions kind=method
  digest=b3:a03176e76f9ee75e0eeda593d36cd98cbce255300f928a272f7fb6d061db7f61 file=layerx/internal/store/store.go range=88:125 lang=go exported=true byte_range=2939:4637
  sig=func (s *Store) EnsureTransferPartitions(ctx context.Context) error
  doc=EnsureTransferPartitions creates the seq-range partitions of the (partitioned)\ntransfers table up to well ahead of the current high-water seq, so inserts\nalways land in a concrete partition rather than the DEFAULT overflow safety\nnet. Idempotent (CREATE ... IF NOT EXISTS), cheap (instant DDL), and safe to\ncall at boot + on a periodic ticker. A no-op on PG installs where transfers is\nnot yet partitioned (pre-005): the CREATE ... PARTITION OF would error, so we\nfirst confirm the table is partitioned.
EDGES
  ^contains=github.com/paxlabs-inc/layerx/internal/store.Store
  ^defines=github.com/paxlabs-inc/layerx/internal/store/store.go

